PASS  B3.rebind resolver returns BOTH orderings (permitted-first=7, forbidden-first=5)
  attempts=100 success(permitted address)=50 tls_error(forbidden address)=49 http_status_codes={'200': 50}
  (successes are the connections the resolver pointed at 172.28.0.60; refusals are the
   connections it pointed at 127.0.0.1. Both outcomes from ONE name prove the decision
   was made on the resolved address.)
PASS  B3.rebind the forbidden address was refused at least once (tls_error=49)
PASS  B3.rebind the permitted answer was NOT collateral damage (it still succeeded 50x)
  note: a success proves the connection reached the IoT Mock (an mTLS handshake
        against 127.0.0.1 inside the node container cannot produce HTTP 200).

